# Geo-Maritime Translator

> Part of [LoPAS Open Translator Core](../LoPAS-Open-Translator-Core)

Translates geopolitical events and maritime traffic into common state space.

---

## Data Sources

| Source | Data | Update |
|--------|------|--------|
| GDELT | News events, conflict density, sentiment | 15 min |
| AIS | Vessel positions, route changes, density | Real-time |
| CMEMS | Sea state, current | 3–6h |

---

## Schema

```yaml
meta:
  translator: geo-maritime-translator
  version: 0.1.0
  timestamp:
  lag_seconds:
  coverage_gap:
  confidence:

coordinate:
  lat:
  lon:
  timestamp:

sources:
  - provider: GDELT
    update_interval: 900    # 15 min
  - provider: AIS
    update_interval: 60     # real-time
  - provider: CMEMS
    update_interval: 10800

observation:
  news_density:             # events per region per hour
  conflict_event_count:
  vessel_density:           # ships per 100km²
  route_change_rate:        # % vessels deviating from normal route
  chokepoint_utilization:   # 0.0–1.0

derived:
  propagation_velocity:     # speed of event impact spreading (km/h)
  route_disruption_risk:    # 0.0–1.0
  chokepoint_pressure:      # 0.0–1.0
  information_lag:          # gap between AIS behavior and GDELT reporting

state:
  status:                   # SAFE | CAUTION | WARNING | CRITICAL
  geopolitics_score:        # 0.0–1.0
  trend:                    # IMPROVING | STABLE | DEGRADING | UNKNOWN

lopas:
  G_cog:  # information gravity — where attention concentrates
  SCI:    # system crisis from conflict / disruption
  CDI:    # vessel distribution — chokepoint concentration
  CPTI:   # phase transition — sudden route change signal
  OSI:    # over-reliance on news vs actual vessel behavior

action:
  recommendation:           # HOLD | MONITOR | REROUTE | ESCALATE
  confidence:
```

---

## Key Signal: AIS before GDELT

The most important pattern this Translator detects:

```yaml
observation:
  route_change_rate: high     # vessels are avoiding an area
  news_density: low           # nothing in the news yet

derived:
  information_lag: high

lopas:
  OSI: elevated
  CPTI: elevated

interpretation: >
  Ships are moving before the news breaks.
  This is the earliest geopolitical signal available from open data.
```

This pattern appeared before multiple Red Sea escalations.  
It is the open-data equivalent of LoPAS "Observation Space Shock."

